// ── SFN-765 nameConstraints fixtures (RFC 5280 §4.2.1.10) ──
//
// Independently rooted from every other family in this file: `fx_nx_inter`'s
// private key was discarded when that fixture was committed, so a leaf that
// verifies under it cannot be produced here. `nc_root` is a fresh Ed25519 CA
// (pathlen:2) purpose-built for this family; `nc_root2` is a second,
// separately rooted anchor for the two-level cases (5/6) that need the
// anchor itself, not just an intermediate, to carry constraints.
//
//   nc_inter_permits_corp          permitted DNS:corp.example
//   nc_inter_permits_excl          permitted DNS:corp.example, excluded DNS:secret.corp.example
//   nc_inter_excludes_evil         excluded DNS:evil.corp.example only
//   nc_inter_permits_ip            permitted IP:10.0.0.0/255.0.0.0
//   nc_inter_permits_corp_noncrit  permitted DNS:corp.example, non-critical
//   nc_inter_dirname               permitted directoryName (unsupported form)
//   nc_inter_rfc822                excluded rfc822Name (unsupported form)
//   nc_root2 -> nc_subca           nc_root2 permits corp.example; nc_subca
//                                  permits both corp.example and example.com
//
// `openssl verify` was run against every inter/leaf pair below (trusting the
// relevant root, `-untrusted` the intermediate) and agrees with the expected
// outcome in every case except the wildcard-exclusion pair (nc_leaf_c7 under
// nc_inter_excludes_evil): OpenSSL's own nameConstraints checker accepts it,
// which is the naive strict-match behaviour SFN-765's test explicitly targets
// (row 7 of the design's test matrix) — this module deliberately diverges
// there. `nc_leaf_c15` (a leaf asserting its own nameConstraints) has no
// OpenSSL cross-check because path validation, not parsing, is what rejects
// it. Decision 6: the self-issued-intermediate exemption (RFC 5280 §6.1.4)
// is not implemented, so `_name_constraints_code` checks every certificate
// below an issuer with no rollover carve-out — the stricter direction — and
// this file carries no rollover fixture.
